Title: Parallel Future Backend using 'callr'
Authors@R: c(person("Henrik", "Bengtsson",
                    role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
                    email = "henrikb@braju.com",
                    comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-7579-5165")))
Description: Implementation of the Future API <doi:10.32614/RJ-2021-048> on
    top of the 'callr' package. The backend is fully compliant with the
    Future API, as validated by the 'future.tests' conformance test suite,
    meaning that code using futures gives identical results and behaves the
    same regardless of which future backend is used. Each future is resolved
    in a fresh background R session on the local machine, and, contrary to
    backends relying on the 'parallel' package and socket connections, it
    can run more than 125 parallel R processes. A common use is to
    parallelize existing map-reduce calls via the 'futurize' package
    <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2601.17578>, e.g. 'plan(future.callr::callr)'
    followed by 'lapply(xs, fcn) |> futurize()' or
    'purrr::map(xs, fcn) |> futurize()'.
